&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next Billing Operations Analyst.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio is looking for a talented and results driven person who is passionate about work, savvy about billing and pricing from the business view not only financial and who lives&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt; the Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt; They also have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Outstanding communication skills, both written and verbal, and ability to advocate for a position while maintaining a collaborative, and open-minded approach. You should be someone who is a champion of streamlining processes and sees projects through to completion. We are looking for someone who enjoys and thrives in a fast-paced environment, with zealous attention to detail, good judgment, and is dedicated to providing excellent customer service.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain Revenue Team external customer email, responding to customer and other external queries in a timely manner and onboard customers to Twilio’s internal billing system and Financial ERP system, Gather and format large raw data sets to assist with customer billing reporting and queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in month end close, including: Managing and tracking recurring billing and managing approvals, tracking and application of customer credits. Analysis of revenue related balance sheet accounts, Ad hoc customer financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist and participate in the development and implementation of financial controls and process surrounding revenue and invoicing, Onboard customers to Twilio’s internal billing system and Financial ERP system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in external and internal audits, as requested.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve queries customers are facing relating to their billing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently investigate customer issues, searching internal resources, previous cases, Slack channels etc to understand issues and provide detailed analysis of customer issues to the Sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manipulate and analyze large datasets in Excel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to the Sales team in a timely manner and communicate complicated issues via Slack, via SFDC, via calls. Excellent communication skills are required - occasional calls with customers or Senior Leaders may be required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work under pressure - high paced environment, quick turnaround times in order to comply with team SLA’s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other teams in order to solve root problems to customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help out on other teams within the Billing Ops group, as requested&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in Month End close, as requested.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in the area of Billings / Revenue / Order to Cash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving, strong interpersonal and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Oracle, Zuora and Salesforce is advantageous, although not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience working with large volume transactions with strong attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel user: able to handle very large raw data sets using pivots and other functions such as VLOOKUPS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years experience in an Operations role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Periodic weekend work will also be essential for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient Spanish and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third level qualification in Accountancy, Finance or a Business related discipline or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote, and based in&amp;nbsp; Mexico City Mexico.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportuniti

&lt;h1&gt;Growth at HRtechX&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world’s most demanding investors are busy managing trillions, and ignore anything average. Are you excited by the challenge of making them act?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you looking to work in an exceptional entrepreneurial team with ambitious, motivated and extremely driven people? And do you want real ownership from your first week? If so, now is the time to apply for the Growth role at Private Equity Insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mission: build the world&#39;s largest network for private equity investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in sprints and get fast execution under your skin. AI has completely changed the game: You will learn to deploy it to outperform a marketing team of 20+ people, while also learning the fundamentals of copywriting that makes elite investors act, get it to the right investor at a meaningful frequency and deploy what works across every marketing channel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want an ambitious mission, real ownership and the fastest learning curve of your career: apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why HRtechX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HRtechX is a world leading HRtech community, connecting industry executives, entrepreneurs and professionals. We are a start-up on a growth journey who help leaders evolve and create stronger businesses through people and technology. We aim to address the challenges and opportunities for HR and HR Tech. We bring together the most influential executives, investors, and entrepreneurs to share their insights on how technology will shape the future of HR, as well as forge long lasting partnerships and client relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HRtechX is part of United Media (&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.united-media.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.united-media.com/&lt;/a&gt;) which focuses on building large scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, HR, private equity, retail, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master the highest bar in the world.&lt;/strong&gt; Our audience is the world&#39;s most demanding investors. They ignore anything average. If your work can make them act, you can make anyone act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unlimited growth potential. &lt;/strong&gt;You will get responsibility before you feel ready. That is how you grow fast. We strongly believe in and have a track record of promoting internally. You can expect coaching and development from leaders, peers and experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills that compound for life.&lt;/strong&gt; Fast execution, copywriting, pricing, conversion optimisation, structured problem solving, and the ability to create impact anywhere in the business at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership from the very start.&lt;/strong&gt; You own outcomes, not tasks. We agree the goal, and you find the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel opportunity.&lt;/strong&gt; You will be joining our 10+ conferences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities in this job will vary, however, feed into the mission: build the world&#39;s largest network for private equity investors. They will be mostly centered around the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the audience.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify, target, and convert every fund into our community, and make sure each one receives the right message, at the right time, and never one too many.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own marketing channels that drive revenue. &lt;/strong&gt;Through existing and new marketing channels, you execute activities that ultimately will drive revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write copy that persuades.&lt;/strong&gt; Every email, landing page and post. Become the best copywriter and leverage it at scale with AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sprint, test, implement.&lt;/strong&gt; Measure the impact of all experiments you run, test offers, copy, prices and pages until the numbers move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build systems, not one-offs.&lt;/strong&gt; Anything you do twice becomes a playbook or an AI workflow, so the next win takes less effort than the last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do whatever it takes to win.&lt;/strong&gt; Some days that means designing an AI workflow. Some days it means checking investors in at the registration desk at 7am. Nobody here is too good for the work that deliver value for investors and fund managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we expect from you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 to 3 years of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Min. a bachelor or master degree with great results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A UK work permit. We do not sponsor visas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong work ethic with a sense of urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional drive and desire to be the best at what you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive approach and sense of ownership/responsibility of everything you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A humble approach and share our passion for building companies and developing people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in continuous learning and proactively searching for ways to optimise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-time, in person from our London office (WeWork), 5 days a week. Expect to travel for work about 20 days a year. The start date is flexible.&lt;/p&gt;
<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gemini is a global crypto and Web3 platform founded by Cameron and Tyler Winklevoss in 2014, offering a wide range of simple, reliable, and secure crypto products and services to individuals and institutions in over 70 countries. Our mission is to unlock the next era of financial, creative, and personal freedom by providing trusted access to the decentralized future. We envision a world where crypto reshapes the global financial system, internet, and money to create greater choice, independence, and opportunity for all — bridging traditional finance with the emerging cryptoeconomy in a way that is more open, fair, and secure. As a publicly traded company, Gemini is poised to accelerate this vision with greater scale, reach, and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Department: Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Prediction Markets Operations team turns real-world events into clearly defined event contracts. We support markets across their full lifecycle—from an initial idea, through configuration and launch, into live operations, and finally to accurate resolution. Our work sits at the intersection of current events, marketplaces, and regulated products, and it demands precision at every step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is responsible for making sure every contract is: clearly and objectively written, based on reliable, authoritative resolution sources, accurately configured, supported with appropriate images and content, thoroughly reviewed before launch, monitored while live, and resolved accurately and consistently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Prediction Markets Operations Intern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a detail-oriented, hands-on internship for someone interested in marketplaces, operations, current events, financial technology, or regulated products. You will perform time-sensitive operational work and learn firsthand how prediction markets move from an idea to a live and, ultimately, settled contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role depends on accuracy, sound judgment, reliability, and operational discipline. Just as important is the willingness to escalate uncertainty rather than guess. You will support, coordinate, research, prepare, review, and execute work under established procedures, working closely with partners across Prediction Markets, Operations, Customer Support, Product, Engineering, Compliance, Legal, Design, Marketing, and our liquidity partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This will be a semester long internship program with 3 days a week in person&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; at our New York City, NY office from January to April 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract Research and Market Listings&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research potential prediction-market contract ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help turn ideas into precise, objective binary questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify reliable and authoritative public resolution sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag ambiguity, potentially prohibited subject matter, or questions requiring Compliance or Legal review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare contract specifications, including outcomes, dates, descriptions, tickers, resolution criteria, and other listing details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and configure event contracts in the Contract Management System, or assist with structured CSV uploads, under established procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support research and documentation related to product requirements and filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Assurance and Launch Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform pre-launch and post-upload quality assurance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify contract names, outcomes, ordering, start times, expiration times, resolution criteria, and designated sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review dates and times carefully, including UTC-based fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare contracts with relevant external prediction markets when appropriate, and identify unintended differences in outcomes, timing, or mechanics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm that event and social images are present and appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upload or update approved event images, social images, and display settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate launch information with internal stakeholders and liquidity partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify discrepancies and escalate issues before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer and Live-Market Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, triage, and investigate prediction-market support tickets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather relevant facts, document findings, and route issues appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor live markets for incorrect content, timing discrepancies, operational issues, or unexpected behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow established incident-escalation procedures when urgent technical or operational issues arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate trackers, checklists, SOPs, and internal documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve repetitive workflows and reduce manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Monitoring and Resolution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor contracts approaching expiration or awaiting resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research outcomes using the contract’s designated resolution source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare a proposed outcome, source links, and a concise rationale for internal review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Double-check resolution information against authoritative sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate unclear, conflicting, delayed, or incomplete source information rather than guessing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute approved market settlements in the Contract Management System after required training, review, and approval.
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Settlement activity is performed only under established procedures, supervision, access controls, and approval requirements. Accuracy is critical, because completed settlements may not be reversible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document completed resolutions according to team procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduled Monitoring Coverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in a scheduled rotation for brief evening or weekend monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is lightweight, scheduled coverage—not continuous or unrestricted on-call work.&

